{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w43yhqljz624cytkykp6b4u5kya3efa7mzgewvtuxsfqmksogshq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass from a clean tree in every configuration.\n\n## What the C actually is\n\n`c_src/` is a single 33-line translation unit exporting three symbols: `find_container_of_a`, `find_container_of_b`, and `main`. `CMakeLists.txt` has no options and the C has no `#ifdef`; `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` — so there is **exactly one** build configuration (verified as `--no-default-features`, default, `--all-features`, plus the `release` profile, rather than assumed).\n\n## Real translation defects found and fixed\n\nThe pre-existing translation was a binary crate with **no exported symbols at all**, so nothing could be differentially tested through the FFI boundary:\n\n1. **`container_of` arithmetic was missing.** `find_container_of_b` had been translated as `fn(&Test) -> &Test { t }` — the `- offsetof(struct test, b)` subtraction was simply gone. Now both functions do real wrapping address arithmetic (`offset_of!` on a `#[repr(C)]` struct), so `find_container_of_b(NULL)` returns `0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC` exactly like the C.\n2. **No C-ABI surface.** Added `src/lib.rs` as a `cdylib` exporting `find_container_of_a`, `find_container_of_b`, and `main` — the same three symbols as the C `.so`, `nm -D` diff now empty.\n3. **`atoi` operated on Rust slices, not C strings**, so the `argv[1] == NULL` crash was emulated by a hand-rolled fault rather than by the actual parse path. It now takes `*const c_char` and faults naturally on NULL.\n4. **SIGPIPE divergence.** Rust's runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN`; the C program inherits `SIG_DFL`. With stdout a reader-less pipe the C died from signal 13 while Rust exited 0. Fixed in `src/main.rs`, and the mutation check confirms the test catches it.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 3/3 exported symbols present; `comm` diff empty; no undefined non-libc symbols; no stubs.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 21 rows. The C has *zero* explicit error handling (grep for `if`/`assert`/`return -1`/`return NULL`/enums finds nothing), so the surface is the faults it permits plus its silent mangling: `strtol` saturation → `(int)` truncation, `argc` never validated, pointer underflow, `printf` failure ignored. All 21 have passing tests; fault rows run in a `fork()`ed child so the exact signal (`SIGSEGV`) is compared, not just \"both failed\".\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 28 rows across pointer-value shapes, `atoi` lexical forms, magnitude classes, `argc` values, stdout kinds, `-O0` vs `-O2` reference builds, and 100 KB inputs.\n\n**54 tests**, all loading both `.so`s via `libloading` and comparing bytes.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **`cargo test` alone does not build the `cdylib`** (no test target depends on it), so tests were silently loading a stale artifact — that's how a mutated `.so` survived a source restore. `check_all_features.sh` now builds first, and `build.rs` provides a fallback so a bare `cargo test` is still meaningful.\n- **`mutation_check.sh` found one vacuous test.** `error_paths` row 6 tested whitespace-*only* input, which cannot detect a wrong `isspace` set (unrecognised bytes also yield 0). Strengthened to check each whitespace byte *in front of digits* plus every non-whitespace control byte; all 9 mutations are now caught."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":166806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":962,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c69d8f8-ba4f-40b9-9dfe-87cdbf050c2c","uuid":"deefc937-33f3-4eed-ad15-5676dd7823cb","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:31:50.981Z"}
